# Milestone: M5
# Covers: D-slotchange-3 determinism rule (spec #4 §7): a sync slot-change
#         handler that triggers a nested slot-change write degrades to async
#         (deferred ring); the deferred entry is dispatched at the next
#         safepoint before watcher_eval_dirty, producing deterministic output.
#
# blocked: at.sync not implemented + string concat (T46 dropped)
# matrix-row: reactive-slot-change
#
# Reason:
#   The fixture requires:
#     - var declaration at top level (globals exposure, T69)
#     - Object.new() constructor (globals + stdlib, T70+)
#     - at sync (obj.x.changed?) watcher (globals for `obj`)
#     - at (obj.y.changed?) watcher
#     - obj.x = N assignment (globals for `obj`)
#   All require the T69 globals-exposure task.  The underlying deferred-ring
#   drain and reentrancy degrade are tested in unit/test_slot_change_reentrancy.c.
#
# Activate at T69 by replacing the source below with the uncommented version.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T69):
#   var o = Object.new();
#   var log = "";
#   at sync (o.x.changed?) function (v) { o.y = v + 100 };
#   at (o.y.changed?) function (v) { log = log + "Y" + v };
#   o.x = 1;
#   echo(log);
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "Y101"
